# Build-context filter for infra/e2e/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` before the context root's
# `.dockerignore`, so this file governs `docker build -f infra/e2e/Dockerfile .`
# and nothing else. That is deliberate: the repository root has no
# `.dockerignore`, this is the only image built from the root as context, and a
# root-level file would be a shared surface that another tool's Compose build
# would silently inherit.
#
# Everything excluded here is either reproduced inside the image (node_modules,
# dist) or has no business in it (history, scratch state, secrets). Without the
# first two the context is about a gigabyte and the daemon spends longer
# receiving it than the install takes.

# Reproduced by `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` inside the image, for Linux
# rather than for this laptop: node_modules here holds the darwin-arm64 Remotion
# compositor and the darwin esbuild, neither of which can run in the container.
**/node_modules

# Reproduced by `pnpm turbo build`. Copying a host build in would also copy the
# turbo cache that says it is up to date.
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/out
**/release
**/.next

# Local toolchains and caches, none of them portable to the image.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
infra/terraform/.terraform

# History, scratch state and machine-local settings. `.session/` is where the
# run's own artefacts land on the host; sending them into the build would make
# every run's context depend on the previous run's output.
.git
.github
.session
.omc
.env
**/.DS_Store
